--
Both threads are joined right after they are created, so the front end turns
each into a plain call in the thread that creates it (goto_convert_functions,
the create/join collapse), and the trace runs everything as thread 0. The
program still has three threads, and reach_error() is called by the third: the
witness has to register both threads at their pthread_create and put the
target in thread 2, or a validator looks for the call in main.
